      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "The vectors of random effects can have different dimensions $ (q_1 \\text{ for } \\mathbf{u}_1, q_2 \\text{ for } \\mathbf{u}_2) $, so with $ n $ individuals in the vector $ \\mathbf{y} $, the incidence matrix $ \\mathbf{Z}_i $ is $ n \\times q_i $ (for $ i = 1, 2 $). Letting $ \\mathbf{R} $ be the $ n \\times n $ covariance matrix for the vector of residual errors $ \\mathbf{e} $, and $ \\mathbf{G}_i $ be the $ q_i \\times q_i $ covariance matrix for $ \\mathbf{u}_i $, the MMEs become",
